# SPDX-License-Identifier: CC-BY-4.0
#
# The EXACT output of the native producer math::producers::onnx_lift (dogfooded — this
# fixture IS what the producer emits, byte for byte after the SPDX header block).
# onnx_lift runs the shipped executable ONNX front-end, gmeow_math_lift::onnx::lift —
# the same entrypoint the `gmeow` CLI calls — over the real committed artifact
# crates/math-lift/fixtures/mlp.onnx, embedded in the binary at compile time, and mints
# under the producer namespace. Nothing here is hand-authored: every triple was decoded
# from the protobuf wire format by the hand-written ModelProto reader and lifted.
#
# The run is a math:ONNXIngestRun carrying the four ingest-frame obligations (a retained
# logic:loadBearing math:parseSource witness, logic:instantiatesSchema,
# logic:instantiatesPlan, and a math:ingestCorrespondence whose logic:Correspondence
# holds the whole law spine), and a structured math: codomain of 55 nodes, each
# gmeow:wasGeneratedBy the run — a non-empty lift, clean under math:UnliftableIngest.
# The rung is a lossy lens over a CRISP source (logic:LossyLens / logic:ValidationOnly /
# logic:RelatedMatch / logic:Crisp, logic:mnemomorphic true): operator types, tensor
# shapes, and the opset are exact, while weight PAYLOADS are held by reference and never
# inlined, so the tensor values do not survive the lift.
#
# Drift is a loud failure: crates/math/tests/lift_fixture_drift.rs regenerates the
# producer and byte-compares against this file.

